    "evaluation": [
      {
        "id": "en.n10.c55.e01",
        "format": "escribir",
        "prompt": {
          "es": "Escribe tu charla de cinco minutos: gancho, tres ideas, cierre y respuesta."
        },
        "answer": {
          "text": "Have you ever run so slowly that a walker passed you? That was me, three years ago, on my first morning with the Park Runners club. I was a beginner, I was out of breath, and I wanted to quit. Today I will tell you why I stayed. First, running is not about speed; it is about habit. Moreover, the club gave me friends who waited for me at every corner. Having said that, nobody made me feel small. Second, running changed my head: I am calmer, happier and more patient. Seldom have I felt so proud as on the day I finished my first ten kilometres. Third, it is cheap. You only need shoes and a park. To sum up, run slowly, run with friends and never stop trying. That is my takeaway. And remember the walker who passed me? Last week, I passed him. Thank you for your question: you asked whether you must be fast to join. Not at all; beginners are the heart of our club.",
          "accepted": [
            "Have you ever run so slowly that a walker passed you? That was me, three years ago, on my first morning with the Park Runners club. I was a beginner, I was out of breath, and I wanted to quit. Today I will tell you why I stayed. First, running is not about speed; it is about habit. Moreover, the club gave me friends who waited for me at every corner. Having said that, nobody made me feel small. Second, running changed my head: I am calmer, happier and more patient. Seldom have I felt so proud as on the day I finished my first ten kilometres. Third, it is cheap. You only need shoes and a park. To sum up, run slowly, run with friends and never stop trying. That is my takeaway. And remember the walker who passed me? Last week, I passed him. Thank you for your question: you asked whether you must be fast to join. Not at all; beginners are the heart of our club.",
            "Good evening. Nine out of ten people quit a new sport in the first month. Today I want to show you how to stay. First, choose a sport that you love. Moreover, find a club, because friends make every hour easier. Having said that, you must be patient. Second, practise a little every day. Third, enjoy the small wins. Never have I felt so happy as on the day I finished my first race. Last year, I was a beginner too, and I was afraid of looking silly. Now I look forward to every training. Why wait? Start this week, and you will see. To sum up, be patient, be kind to yourself and have fun. That is my takeaway. Good question, by the way: you asked if it is expensive. Not at all; a pair of shoes is enough."
          ]
        },
